    fix(source-control): draw a patch only when a strict second reading agrees (BBP-51 review 4)
    
    An independent strict pass (core/patch-strict.ts) walks the source once and
    accounts for every line. A patch draws only when it reads strictly and its
    per-file list matches the main reader's: order, paths, kinds and counts.
    Otherwise it shows as text with a reason. Files Pierre can't parse or counts
    short of their headers also fall back to text, and Only in records are never
    dropped. The fuzz oracle now covers mail and log inputs; the reviewer's six
    fixtures and eleven variations are tests.

